    hsCodes:["8541.42.00.00","8541.43.00.00"],
    scopeNote:"Photovoltaic modules and laminates using crystalline silicon cells (including laminates shipped/packaged with other module components), plus thin-film products from amorphous silicon (a-Si), cadmium telluride (CdTe), or copper indium gallium selenide (CIGS), from China. KEY EXCLUSIONS: modules/laminates/thin-film products with power output NOT exceeding 100W; a specific named exception — 195W monocrystalline modules made of exactly 72 monocrystalline cells, each cell no more than 5in x 5in — is excluded despite exceeding 100W; and modules/laminates/thin-film products incorporated into electrical goods whose FUNCTION is something other than power generation (i.e. the solar component just powers the device, isn't the product itself) are excluded. CITT further amended the order March 13, 2026 to exclude certain flexible photovoltaic products — verify current exclusion list for flexible/thin-film variants specifically.",
