// ===== Chapter 28 — Inorganic Chemicals; Organic or Inorganic Compounds of
// Precious Metals, of Rare-Earth Metals, of Radioactive Elements or of
// Isotopes (verified 07 AUG 2026 from CBSA Ch.28, user-provided markdown) =====
// NOT added to MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS — same reasoning as Ch.27: a real
// dutiable exception exists (2852.90.10, mercury albuminate, 6.5% MFN with a
// GPT-specific reduced 3% rate — same shape as the Ch.24 tobacco GPT/CPTPT
// reductions), plus confirmed source gaps in the radioactive-isotopes group
// (natural/enriched/depleted uranium, plutonium, thorium, several named
// isotopes — 2844.10/.20/.30/.42/.43.*, 7 codes) where the extraction lost the
// rate line entirely with nothing nearby to infer from. Left out of MFN_RATES
// so they honestly return null.
//
// Two garbled-but-recoverable regions, resolved by exact count-matching
// (N orphaned codes with no attached rate, immediately followed by exactly N
// floating Free rate blocks before the next real subheading — same displaced-
// block pattern as Ch.25-27, just spanning a wider gap here): the phosphorus/
// sulphur chloride group (2812.14 through 2813.90, 8 codes) and the
// molybdenum/antimony-oxide group (2825.70/.80/.90, 3 codes). Both inferred
// Free with high confidence given the exact count match and the chapter's
// otherwise unbroken Free pattern (300+ of ~305 codes are Free).
//
// 2804.69.00.00 (silicon, other) already has an MFN_RATES entry from an
// earlier session (tied to the Silicon Metal SIMA case against China) — not
// re-added here, only its CODE_DESCRIPTIONS entry was missing and is added.
//
// Notable but NOT structurally special: several codes (2823 titanium oxides,
// 2824 lead oxides, 2835.22-.39 phosphates) list AUT/NZT (Australia/New
// Zealand bilateral treaties) alongside the usual list — first appearance of
// those treaty codes outside Chapter 4. Since MFN itself is already Free on
// all of these, it doesn't change how they're encoded (no PREF_FREE needed
// either way), just worth knowing AUT/NZT exist and are already valid keys.

