// Section I (39.01-39.14, primary-form resins) is 100% Free throughout — raw
// plastic resin, matching the same duty-free-feedstock pattern as Ch.28/29's
// raw chemicals. Section II runs the same 6.5%/GPT-3% pattern seen across
// Ch.32-38, with dozens of specific manufacturing-end-use exemptions (Free)
// scattered throughout — standard CBSA pattern, not chapter-specific.
// One 3-way split found: 3926.90.30 (signs/letters/numerals) at
// AUT-5.5%/NZT-5.5%/GPT-3%.
// Built around 6 pre-existing stray codes from earlier SIMA/surtax-case work
// (3907.61/3907.69.* — PET resin SIMA case, both Free, matching this read;
// 3925.20.00.10/.90 — door/window frames surtax order, 6.5%, matching this
// read) — none re-added to MFN_RATES, only their missing CODE_DESCRIPTIONS
// and (for the 3925.20 pair) PREF_FREE/PREF_SPECIAL entries, since only the
// bare MFN rate existed previously with no preferential resolution.
// No gaps — one genuinely ambiguous spot (3917.33/3917.39.10, where a 6.5%
// block and a Free block appeared out of naive sequential order) was resolved
// by matching content, not position: 3917.39.10 carries the identical
// exemption-list content as the confirmed-Free 3917.32.10, so it was assigned
// Free and the 6.5% block to 3917.33 instead of blindly taking blocks in the
// order they appeared on the page.

