// ===== Chapter 44 — Wood and Articles of Wood; Wood Charcoal (verified 09
// AUG 2026 from CBSA Ch.44, user-provided markdown, 1,592-line source, full
// read) =====
// Free-by-default (added to MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS) — 213 of 262 codes
// Free (81%), concentrated entirely in Section I (raw/rough/sawn lumber,
// 44.01-44.13), which is essentially 100% duty-free regardless of species —
// the extensive per-species/grade statistical breakdowns in 44.03 and 44.07
// (pine, fir/spruce, oak, birch, maple, etc., each split into dressed/rough,
// pulpwood/poles/other) all share the identical Free rate; only ONE code in
// the entire raw-lumber section is dutiable (4409.29.10, oak flooring, 3.5%).
// Section II (articles — frames, packing cases, doors, windows, tableware,
// engineered structural timber) carries the real dutiable content.
//
// Worth flagging: this chapter closely interleaves two DIFFERENT GPT
// treatments on codes that otherwise look similar, and it's easy to cross
// the two up (an earlier pass on this exact chapter did, and got corrected
// before shipping) — some headings (44.09 oak flooring, 44.11 MDF 'other',
// 44.17 tool handles, 44.18 windows/doors/shuttering/flooring panels/
// engineered timber) list GPT directly in the main Free-for-everyone treaty
// list (no special needed), while others sitting right nearby (44.14 picture
// frames, 44.15 packing cases, 44.19 tableware, 44.20 ornaments, 44.21 other
// articles) explicitly exclude GPT from that list and give it its own reduced
// rate instead. Don't assume one pattern from a neighboring heading.
// Two 3-way AUT/NZT/GPT splits: 4421.91.20 and 4421.99.20 (blinds/labels/
