// ===== Chapter 61 - Articles of Apparel and Clothing Accessories, Knitted
// or Crocheted (verified 10 AUG 2026 from CBSA Ch.61, user-provided
// markdown, 1,646-line source, full read) =====
// NOT free-by-default - overwhelmingly dutiable (169 of 178 codes, 95%),
// the most extreme dutiable-majority chapter in this entire build. Standard
// pattern throughout: 18% MFN with GPT almost universally excluded (zero
// relief), and AUT/NZT getting 11% relief on MOST but not all codes -
// several material categories (wool, and 'other textile materials' in
// several headings) get NO AUT/NZT relief either, stuck at the full 18%
// same as GPT. Don't assume AUT/NZT relief is universal within a heading -
// it varies code by code even within the same garment type.
// Rare exception to the GPT-zero-relief pattern: high-value wool/cashmere
// women's jerseys valued >= $20/kg (6110.11.10, 6110.12.10, 6110.19.10) get
// a real GPT discount to 16%, unlike the 'other' (non-high-value) variants
// right next to them which get zero GPT relief.
// Babies' garments (61.11) are the one heading that's entirely Free -
// matches a common real-world tariff pattern of relief for children's
// clothing. A handful of scattered manufacturing/protective-use exemptions
// (protective suits for noxious atmospheres, prayer shawls, diving suit
// parts) are Free even within otherwise-dutiable headings.
// Hosiery (61.15) and gloves (61.16) run their own distinct rate shapes
// (16% and 18% respectively, with different special-rate patterns) rather
// than the 61.01-61.14 apparel-wide 18%/AUT11/NZT11 shape - don't assume
// uniformity across the whole chapter.

