// ===== Chapter 63 - Other Made Up Textile Articles; Sets; Worn Clothing and
// Worn Textile Articles; Rags (verified 10 AUG 2026 from CBSA Ch.63,
// user-provided markdown, 827-line source, full read) =====
// NOT free-by-default - overwhelmingly dutiable (80 of 84 codes, 95%),
// consistent with the finished-textile-article pattern from Ch.61/62.
// Free exceptions genuinely cluster at the chapter's end: worn clothing
// specifically for wiping-rag manufacturing (6309.00.10) and both grades of
// used/new rags (63.10, sorted and unsorted alike) are Free, while ordinary
// worn clothing (6309.00.90) is dutiable at 18% - a real distinction between
// 'worn clothing sold as clothing' and 'worn clothing destined for rag/wipe
// manufacturing' that's easy to miss. A cluster of scattered manufacturing/
// safety-use exemptions also stay Free within 6307.90 (climbing harnesses,
// marine evacuation chutes, NIOSH respirators, burial shrouds).
// 'Seat covers for motor vehicles' gets a distinctly lower flat rate (15.5%)
// across every material variant in 63.04 (knitted, cotton, synthetic, other)
// compared to the 17-18% general rate for the same heading otherwise -
// consistent, not a one-off.
// One duplicated-CCCT extraction artifact noted on the seat-cover codes
// (CCCT appears twice in the source's treaty list) - harmless, resolved as
// the standard FULL_MINUS_GPT pattern since the actual treaty SET is
// unambiguous despite the duplication.

