// read) =====
// This chapter had only partial prior coverage (50 scattered MFN_RATES
// entries from 73.02 onward, zero descriptions, large stretches of 73.01 and
// 73.04-73.14 completely uncovered) - not a verified pass like Ch.72, so it
// was rebuilt in full rather than just backfilled. The 50 pre-existing rates
// were spot-checked against this source during the build and confirmed
// correct (7307.29.20 at 4.5%, the 73.19-73.21 series, etc.) - re-declared
// here with matching values, not silently trusted.
// Free-by-default (added to MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS) - 56 of 483 codes
// dutiable (12%). Clean structural split: 73.01-73.18 (structures, pipe,
// fittings, tanks, wire rope, chain, mesh, nails, threaded fasteners) is
// almost entirely Free; 73.19-73.26 (needles/pins, springs, non-electric
// appliances, cookware, sanitary ware, cast/forged articles, other) carries
// nearly all the dutiable content - the finished-consumer-goods pattern seen
// throughout this build.
// The overwhelming majority of the code count comes from three headings
// (73.04-73.06, oil/gas line pipe and well casing/tubing) which repeat
// massive API-grade x diameter-bracket suffix tables many times over - all
// genuinely Free at the MFN level, captured at full statistical-suffix
// precision per request, but structurally repetitive rather than reflecting
// product diversity the way Ch.72's size did.

