// ===== Chapter 85 - Electrical Machinery and Equipment and Parts Thereof;
// Sound Recorders and Reproducers, Television Image and Sound Recorders
// and Reproducers, and Parts and Accessories of Such Articles (verified 10
// AUG 2026 from CBSA Ch.85, user-provided markdown, 4,622-line source, full
// read, complete chapter 85.01-85.49) =====
// Free-by-default (added to MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS) - 100 of 612 codes
// dutiable (16%). Two pre-existing verified stray codes (8541.42, 8541.43,
// photovoltaic cells) independently confirmed correct against this source.
// Distinct pattern from Ch.84: mostly Free like industrial machinery, but
// with real, meaningful dutiable pockets concentrated in specific consumer
// goods categories rather than one uniform rate. Batteries/accumulators
// (85.06-85.07) carry real duty (7%) on general-purpose cells, with
// consistent Free carve-outs for EV/motorcycle power, smoke detectors,
// electronic locks and safety lamps. Small appliances (85.08-85.13, 85.16)
// carry real duty (3-9%) with specific Free carve-outs by appliance type
// (bread makers, rice cookers, automatic toasters, microwave ovens sit right
// next to dutiable general categories). Telecommunications/broadcast/audio
// equipment (85.17-85.27, 85.29-85.45) is almost entirely Free, matching the
// global electronics-liberalization pattern - the major exception is
// television/monitor/projector display technology (85.28), the most
// structurally complex heading in the chapter, with real GPT-relief
// distinctions between near-identical codes based on screen size, finish
// (projection vs non-projection) and completeness. Lighting (85.39) carries
// meaningful duty (2-8%) across most lamp/LED types.
