// ===== Chapter 90 - Optical, Photographic, Cinematographic, Measuring,
// Checking, Precision, Medical or Surgical Instruments and Apparatus;
// Parts and Accessories Thereof (verified 11 AUG 2026 from CBSA Ch.90,
// user-provided markdown, 1,829-line source, full read) =====
// Free-by-default (added to MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS) - only 33 of 240
// codes dutiable (14%). Consistent with a global pattern of not tariffing
// precision scientific/medical equipment: the entire medical/surgical/
// dental/veterinary heading (90.18, the largest in the chapter at 32
// codes), orthopaedic appliances and artificial body parts (90.21), X-ray/
// radiation apparatus (90.22), microscopes, lasers, navigation instruments,
// surveying instruments, gas/liquid/electricity meters, and essentially all
// electrical measuring/testing/automatic-control instruments (90.25-90.33)
// are 100% Free with zero exceptions. The dutiable content concentrates
// almost entirely in consumer optical goods and general-purpose tools:
// spectacle lenses/frames, sunglasses, cameras and their flash/projector
// accessories, drafting tables and tapes/callipers, non-clinical
// thermometers, and general-purpose thermostats. A recurring pattern within
// those dutiable headings: the hazardous-work-safety or medical/surgical-use
// variant of a product is Free, while the general consumer version of the
// exact same product is dutiable (e.g. safety goggles for hazardous work vs.
// sunglasses; medical examination cameras vs. ordinary cameras).
const CH90_FREE_DEFAULT = ["90"];
MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS.push(...CH90_FREE_DEFAULT);

