// ===== Chapter 94 - Furniture; Bedding, Mattresses, Mattress Supports,
// Cushions and Similar Stuffed Furnishings; Luminaires and Lighting
// Fittings, Not Elsewhere Specified or Included; Illuminated Signs,
// Illuminated Name-Plates and the Like; Prefabricated Buildings (verified
// 12 AUG 2026 from CBSA Ch.94, user-provided markdown, 1,008-line source,
// full read) =====
// Free-by-default (added to MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS) - 93 of 150 codes
// dutiable (62%), a genuine dutiable-majority chapter. 22 pre-existing
// stray codes all independently confirmed correct against this source
// (including two orphaned generic bare-.00 suffix keys, 9403.10.00.00 and
// 9403.99.00.00, that don't correspond to real suffixes in this source -
// same harmless pattern as Ch.76/Ch.83; both directions independently
// confirm Free, left in place per this build's pure-append practice).
// Key patterns: seats/furniture consistently split by end-use and
// material - 'for domestic purposes' variants are dutiable while
// commercial/institutional and manufacturing-input variants of the exact
// same product are Free (e.g. wooden domestic chairs dutiable at 9.5% vs.
// the same chair shape for other end-uses Free); office furniture (metal or
// wood) is Free while home furniture in the identical material is dutiable.
// Bedding/cushions (94.04) are broadly dutiable once stuffed/fitted,
// notably including a flat 14% rate across nearly all cotton and non-cotton
// pillows/cushions/quilts regardless of filling type. Lighting (94.05) is
// dutiable at a consistent 7% MFN/5% GPT across LED and non-LED fixtures
// alike, except parts (glass/plastic/other) which are Free. Prefabricated
// buildings (94.06) are dutiable at 4.5-15.5% with a Free carve-out
// specifically for unassembled fibreglass silo components for manufacture.
const CH94_FREE_DEFAULT = ["94"];
MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS.push(...CH94_FREE_DEFAULT);

