// ===== Chapter 95 - Toys, Games and Sports Requisites; Parts and
// Accessories Thereof (verified 12 AUG 2026 from CBSA Ch.95,
// user-provided markdown, full read) =====
// Free-by-default (added to MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS) - only 9 of 100
// codes dutiable (9%). Toys, video games, festive/carnival articles,
// nearly all sports equipment (skis, water-sports gear, golf, table-tennis,
// tennis rackets specifically, hockey/archery/pools/playground equipment),
// and amusement park/fairground/circus equipment are all 100% Free.
// Dutiable content is narrowly concentrated in: ride-on wheeled toys for
// children (8%), general 'other' rackets outside tennis/squash/badminton/
// racketball (7%), skates sold unattached to boots (5.5%), and most of the
// fishing tackle heading (rods, reels, retail fishing line, general tackle,
// 6.5-7%) - though fish-hooks themselves and commercial-fishing-use lures/
// lines stay Free within that same heading.
