// ===== Chapter 96 - Miscellaneous Manufactured Articles (verified 12 AUG
// 2026 from CBSA Ch.96, user-provided markdown, 858-line source, full
// read) =====
// Free-by-default (added to MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS) - 64 of 91 codes
// dutiable (70%), a genuinely dutiable-majority grab-bag chapter covering
// brushes/brooms, buttons/zippers, pens/pencils, lighters, pipes, combs,
// sanitary articles, and monopods/tripods. Manufacturing-input exemptions
// recur throughout (pen nibs/refill parts, pencil leads, meerschaum pipe
// blocks). One genuinely ambiguous extraction case: 9619.00.10 (adult
// incontinence articles) had four floating rate blocks following its own
// text with no other code positioned to claim them; resolved to the nearest
// block (12%, GPT relief to 8%) per this build's established nearest-block
// convention, since the other three candidates didn't cleanly map to any
// other code either. One resolved displaced-block case: heading 96.10
// (slates and boards) had no visible rate of its own, recovered from the
// first of two consecutive blocks following 9611.00.00's text (4.5%, full
// relief), with the second block (6.5%, GPT:5%) confirmed as 9611.00.00's
// own rate. Baby diapers/napkins (9619.00.22-29) show a real, consistent
// pattern of excluding both CCCT and GPT from relief (unlike almost
// everywhere else in this build, where GPT alone is typically excluded) -
// LDCT and the FTA partners still get relief, but least-developed-country
// and general-preferential treatment do not extend to this specific
// product.
const CH96_FREE_DEFAULT = ["96"];
MFN_FREE_DEFAULT_CHAPTERS.push(...CH96_FREE_DEFAULT);

